source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira reads the row on past the end of its line with no forced newline in front of the break: it renders one data cell holding `a`, a break and `b`. A GFM cell is one line, so jiro keeps the whole table as raw Jira Markup.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|a
b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a<br/>
b</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|a
b|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
